US-002 is done and the bead is closed, with two gaps: I skipped the real-browser screenshot check, and the "profile" page type has no page to cover.

- **Handle:** with `tags-atlas` on, a `.atlas-layer-handle` appears right before `#grid-mount`. It has `role="button"`, an `aria-label`, `aria-expanded` and `tabindex="0"`, and is 20px tall. The code is in `atlasLayerHandle.ts`, and `GridPager.arm()` mounts it, so no page-specific code was needed. `disarm()` and `destroy()` remove it. With the plugin off, nothing is added.
- **CSS:** the handle styles are in `frontend/css/public/atlas.css`, and I rebuilt the bundles with `scripts/build-css.sh`.
- **E2E:** `frontend/e2e/atlas-layer.test.ts` checks the handle on home, tag and search, and checks that it is absent when the plugin is off. The "off" test uses a fresh browser context, because a reused one kept the old plugin list.
- **Checks:** `scripts/run-e2e.sh` passes and `scripts/check.sh` passes except `go-test`. `go-test` failed once with a migration "context canceled" error. I changed no Go code, and `go test ./cmd/api` passes on re-run, but I did not re-run the full `scripts/check.sh` afterwards.
- **Trusted Types:** my first version of the handle used `innerHTML`, and the Trusted Types e2e test caught it. It now builds the grip with DOM calls.

The handle does nothing on click yet. Tap and swipe gestures come in US-006 and US-007, and the notes are appended to `.ralph-tui/progress.md`.

The routes here are `/`, `/tags/:slug` and `/search`, so there is no profile page for the handle to appear on.

